       This program is part of NNeettppbbmm(1).

       ppggmmccrraatteerr is obsolete.  All it does now is invoke ppaammccrraatteerr,  ppaammsshhaaddee‐‐
       ddrreelliieeff, and ppaammttooppnnmm.  You should use those programs in any new appli‐
       cation, or if you are modifying an old program or process that does not
       have  to  work  with a version of Netpbm before 10.68 (September 2014).
       ppggmmccrraatteerr exists only for backward compatibility.

       The combination of the three programs mentioned above performs the same
       function as traditional ppggmmccrraatteerr.

       ppggmmccrraatteerr's  --nnuummbbeerr,  --hheeiigghhtt,  --wwiiddtthh,  and  --rraannddoommsseeeedd  options are
       equivalent to the options of the same name on ppaammccrraatteerr.

       ppggmmccrraatteerr's --ggaammmmaa option is equivalent to the option of the same  name
       on ppaammsshhaaddeeddrreelliieeff.

       ppggmmccrraatteerr's  --yyssiizzee option is identical to --hheeiigghhtt; --xxssiizzee is identical
       to --wwiiddtthh.

       Note: The former ppggmmccrraatteerr code was split into ppaammccrraatteerr and  ppaammsshhaaddee‐‐
       ddrreelliieeff.   The reason for the split is that having separate programs is
       more consistent with Netpbm's building block philosophy.  It is  possi‐
       ble the separate components can be used in other applications.



